    "A numerator tells you how many of those equal intervals to move from zero. Five eighths means five eighth-sized steps from zero.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-4a8db32ad78ae4bc.mp3" },
    "The same idea keeps going beyond one. One whole is four quarters, so one quarter past one is five quarters from zero.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-51f7fb2dd2169949.mp3" },
    "Read this point by counting equal intervals from zero.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-923c17a80654791f.mp3" },
    "Denominator sets the interval size; numerator counts the intervals travelled. Tick marks are only boundaries.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-8613a114acbca0fe.mp3" },
    "Now take the idea past one and keep counting the same-sized fractional intervals.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-a685dada859c2aa2.mp3" },
