    "Fractions can be written in different forms, and the form tells us something about the size of the number.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-ad863928df886ade.mp3" },
    "A proper fraction has a numerator smaller than its denominator, so the value is less than one whole.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-750eef9cea2b7118.mp3" },
    "Classify this one by comparing numerator and denominator.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-b04fcbba1b4e3d42.mp3" },
    "An improper fraction has numerator at least as large as the denominator. That includes fractions equal to one, like 6/6.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-ea542d10b3ddc9e1.mp3" },
    "A mixed number writes whole units first and then a proper fractional part, like 2 and 3/5.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-2bee7330ee63a7c6.mp3" },
    "Use those definitions on this boundary case.": { src: "/fractions/audio/ryan-e044217da4a11239.mp3" },
